task #754 — Phase-2 marketplace pilot adapter

Implements the first real adapter on the Phase-2 orchestrator: publish and
unpublish marketplace listings end-to-end (approval → orchestration → lock →
idempotency → execute → verify → events → persist).

What landed
- New verifier-registry.ts framework so verifiers can be looked up per task type.
- Marketplace adapter package: types, policy (lockKey/idempotencyKey/risk),
  listing-repository, kyc-gate, listing-verifier, marketplace-adapter (publish
  + unpublish handlers with previous_state snapshot, post-state verification,
  canonical domain events), bootstrap.
- execution-loop now bootstraps marketplace adapters once at cold start.
- Migration 20260420000000 classifies MARKETPLACE.LISTING.PUBLISH/UNPUBLISH as
  MEDIUM and enforces MEDIUM_REQUIRES_APPROVAL on PUBLISH (UNPUBLISH stays
  SAFE_BY_POLICY/auto).
- In-memory test fakes (MemoryTaskRepository, MemoryListingRepository) shared
  across unit + integration tests.
- 13 unit tests + 5 integration tests (all passing) covering policy, publish,
  unpublish, KYC blocking, invalid payload, listing-not-found, verifier
  mismatch, idempotent double-dispatch and lock collision.
- Runtime proof harness scripts/marketplace-pilot-runtime-proof.ts that drives
  the real ExecutionOrchestratorV2 through five scenarios and writes
  tests/runtime/execution/marketplace-pilot.proof.md with state diffs, event
  timeline, durations and a real-DB playbook.

Notes
- Runtime proof uses the in-memory infra (the same fakes the tests use) so it
  is reproducible in CI without Supabase. The orchestrator code path under
  exercise is identical to production; only persistence/lock/idempotency
  backends differ. A real-DB run is documented as follow-up #791.

Rebase notes
- Resolved conflicts with task #753's verifier framework. Adopted the
  upstream TaskVerifier contract (verify(task, executionResult) → VerifierResult
  with mismatchPath) as the canonical registry shape; the marketplace pilot's
  richer field-diff stays available via the new buildDiff helper appended to
  verifier-registry.ts.
- Refactored listing-verifier.ts to expose two surfaces: a TaskVerifier-shaped
  factory used by TaskVerificationService (orchestrator gate) AND a plain
  verifyExpectedListingState() function the adapter calls directly to produce
  its own VERIFICATION_MISMATCH AdapterResult. Belt-and-suspenders.
- Adapter no longer reads VerifierRegistry; injects verify() helper instead.
- Wired TaskVerificationService into the integration test stack and the
  runtime-proof harness so NO_VERIFIER blocks don't fire. All 18 tests still
  pass; runtime proof regenerated.
- execution-loop keeps both the upstream verification wiring and the
  marketplace bootstrap import.

